     "result_text_tail": "d test of both offers in Q1 2027; if Pro doesn't win twice as many accounts, launch the add-on instead.\n\n**Choices I made for you:**\n- Audience: you and the executive team, approving or rejecting.\n- Theme: navy.\n- I approved the storyline myself, since you weren't available.\n- No checkpoint for missing data: every number comes from the briefing pack.\n\n**What the red-team review changed:** I had a separate agent argue against the draft. It found that the add-on is a strong alternative and that my first allowance (about 850 requests per seat) left no margin room. So I added the \"twice as many accounts\" condition, tightened the allowance to 333, made the add-on the fallback, and corrected the Routewise win-rate gate.\n\n**Numbers:** 122 in total. 55 come straight from the pack, each with its quote and section. 67 are calculations with live Excel formulas in the workbook, 7 of them flagged as estimates. No \"?\" placeholders are left. All data in the pack is synthetic.\n\n**Not costed:** the metering and billing work the allowance needs isn't in the 14-engineer estimate. One of the next steps asks Engineering to confirm in January whether it fits.\n\nPossible next steps: switch the theme, add a backup slide that tests Pro at other price points, or change the gate thresholds if the team prefers different values.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- `brightwork-copilot.pptx`\n- `brightwork-copilot-sources.xlsx`\n- `brightwork-copilot.json`\n\nThe script that builds the spec is `work/build_spec.py`."
